We can optimize this block by retrieving the model instance once via `model = self.get_model()` instead of calling `self.get_model()` repeatedly in each branch.

Additionally, when `load_format is None`, the code calls `model.load_weights(named_tensors)`. Since `load_weights` does not automatically trigger `post_load_weights()`, this branch also bypasses the hook and can serve stale derived weights. Adding the `post_load_weights` check to the `None` branch ensures correctness across all weight-update paths.

```python
        model = self.get_model()
        if load_format == "direct":
            _model_load_weights_direct(model, named_tensors)
            if hasattr(model, "post_load_weights"):
                model.post_load_weights()
        elif load_format in self.custom_weight_loaders:
            custom_loader = dynamic_import(load_format)
            custom_loader(model, named_tensors)
            if hasattr(model, "post_load_weights"):
                model.post_load_weights()
        elif load_format is None:
            model.load_weights(named_tensors)
            if hasattr(model, "post_load_weights"):
                model.post_load_weights()
